=head2 SDL_SetError

  my $result = SDL_SetError($message);

C: C<< _Bool SDL_SetError(const char * fmt, ...) >>

Set the SDL error message for the current thread.

Calling this function will replace any previous error message that was set.

This function always returns false, since SDL frequently uses false to signify a failing result, leading to this idiom:

```c if (error_code) { return SDL_SetError("This operation has failed: %d", error_code); } ```

It is safe to call this function from any thread.

=over

=item message - string, substituted for the format string and its arguments

=back

Returns boolean: false.

Since: This function is available since SDL 3.2.0.

